  "job_B1.3.35_20251001_193219": {
    "text": "XI KAL FEBR, PASSIO SANCTI VINCENTII MARTYRIS.\nON Ispanian lande \u00fe\u00e6re Speoniscan leode w\u00e6s se halga martir \u00fee hatte Uincentius to menn geboren, &\n\u00dea aras seo ehtnys \u00fe\u00e6ra arleasra cweller\u00e6 wide geond \u00feas world wodlice swi\u00f0e ongean Cristes\nOn \u00feam dagum w\u00e6s \u00fea sum heretoga w\u00e6lhreow, Datianus gehatan swi\u00f0e hetol ehtere on anre\nHim geu\u00fee \u00fea se casere, swa swa us cy\u00fea\u00f0 bec, \u00fe\u00e6t se w\u00e6lhreowa ehtere \u00feone anweald h\u00e6fde, \u00fe\u00e6t he\nHw\u00e6t \u00fea Datianus, se deofollica cwellere, on \u00feam anwealde \u00fee he underfangen h\u00e6fde, gecydde his\nWolde \u00e6rest \u00fea heafodmen \u00fe\u00e6s halgan geleafan mid witum oferswi\u00f0an, \u00fe\u00e6t he sy\u00f0\u00f0an mihte \u00fea l\u00e6ssan\n\u00dea efste se bisceop & se eadiga Uincentius to \u00feam \u00e6\u00f0elan martirdome; \u00feohtan \u00fe\u00e6t hi wurdon witodlice\nDatianus \u00fea, se deofollica ehtere, het gebringan \u00fea halgan gebundene mid racenteagum into anre burig\nAnd let hi liggan swa on meteleaste, swi\u00f0e micclum gehefegode mid \u00feam heardan isene; hopode \u00fe\u00e6t hi\n\u00c6fter langsumum fyrste he het hi gebringan him to; wende \u00fe\u00e6t hi w\u00e6ron mid \u00feam witum fornumene,\nHi comon \u00fea begen mid bli\u00f0um mode and mid f\u00e6gerum andwlitum & ansundum lichamum to \u00feam\nHi cw\u00e6don \u00fe\u00e6t hi hym on na\u00feor ne dydon.\nHe ne mihte na tocnaw\u00e6n \u00fe\u00e6t Crist sylf hi afedde, & befran \u00fea mid graman \u00feone fores\u00e6don bisceop,\nAc \u00fee bisceop ne geandwearde \u00feam w\u00e6lhreowum swa hra\u00f0e, for\u00fean \u00fee God wolde \u00fe\u00e6t he wurde\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Uincentius to \u00feam arwyr\u00f0am bisceope \u00feus, La leof, geandweard \u00feam arleasan mid anr\u00e6dum\nSeo ylce n\u00e6dre spec\u00f0 nu \u00feurh \u00feises arleasan mu\u00f0, \u00fee \u00fea frumsceapenan men, Adam and Euan, gefurn\nHe ne geearnode nanes wuldres, ne he ne wunode on so\u00f0f\u00e6stnesse, ac \u00feone dea\u00f0 \u00fee he scencte \u00feam\nWinne he wi\u00fe me on \u00feisum gewinne nu, & he wi\u00f0 me feohte on his feondlicum truwan, & he gesyh\u00f0\n\u00deone ic beo gewitnod \u00feonne he \u00fee witna\u00fe, for\u00fean \u00fee he sylf sceal sw\u00e6rran witu \u00ferowian, & he by\u00f0\n\u00dea geangsumode bealh hine sona se arleasa Datianus, & cw\u00e6\u00f0 to his gingrum & to his witnerum \u00feus,\nAho\u00f0 hine, ic hate, on \u00fe\u00e6re hengene, & hetelice astrecca\u00f0 ealle his lima, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fea li\u00fea him togaan.\n\u00dea gef\u00e6stnodon \u00fea cwelleras \u00feone Cristes \u00feegn on \u00fe\u00e6re heardan hengene, & hine hetelice tihton swa\nHw\u00e6t \u00feing \u00fee be \u00fee sylfuum & be \u00feinum earman lichaman on \u00feysum la\u00feum witum?\nSe halga wer \u00fea cw\u00e6\u00fe to \u00feam w\u00e6lhreowan \u00feus, \u00feises ic gewilnode & gewiscte \u00e6fre.\nNis me nan \u00feing leofre \u00fe\u00e6t me on minum life getimode, & \u00feu swi\u00f0ost ge\u00few\u00e6rl\u00e6cst mines sylfes\nNelle ic \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu geswice, for\u00fean \u00fee ic sylf gearo eom witu to \u00f0rowienne, for \u00feam wuldorfullan Drihtne.\nNelle ic \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0u wanige min wuldor for Gode and mine ges\u00e6l\u00f0a; & \u00feonne \u00feu me witnast, \u00feu bist sylf\nDatianus \u00fea deofollice yrsode, and w\u00e6s gram on his mode, & began to sleanne swi\u00f0e mid gyrdum his\nSe halga wer \u00fea cw\u00e6\u00fe, Nu \u00feu gewrecst on him \u00f0a witu \u00fee ic \u00ferowige for \u00feinre w\u00e6lhreownysse, swilce\nHe hrymde \u00fea swi\u00f0or & mid re\u00f0nysse grymetode swa leo, & gyt swi\u00f0or wedde sleande his cwelleras\n\u00deohte \u00fe\u00e6t he mihte his mod ahnexian \u00feurh \u00fea orm\u00e6tan wita, ac he wann on idel, for\u00fean \u00fee hi\nDatianus \u00fea axode mid \u00e6bl\u00e6cum andwlitan his re\u00f0an cwelleras, \u00feus cwe\u00f0ende him to, Hwar is nu\nNe oncnawe ic eowere handa \u00fee \u00e6fre hetole w\u00e6ran, swa oft swa ge gewitnodon \u00fea \u00f0e w\u00e6ron\n\u00c6fre ge gewyldon mid witum hi ealle, & hi heore diglan d\u00e6da eow bedyrnan ne mihton.\nAc ge nu ne magon \u00feusne mann oferswi\u00f0an \u00fe\u00e6t he huru suwige on \u00feysum scearpum witum.\n\u00dea smercode se halga wer & to \u00feam hetolan Datianus \u00feus cw\u00e6\u00f0, \u00feis is \u00fe\u00e6t awriten is witodlice on\nDrihten Crist ic andette, \u00fe\u00e6s \u00e6lmihtigan f\u00e6der sunu, mid \u00feam halgan gaste, anne so\u00f0ne God.\nAc witna me gyt swi\u00f0or for \u00feissere so\u00f0an andetnysse \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0u on eallum \u00feingum \u00fee oferswi\u00f0edne\nDatianus \u00fea cw\u00e6\u00fe to \u00feam Drihtnes cy\u00feere, gemilsa \u00fee sylfum & ne amyr \u00feine geogu\u00fee, & \u00fein lif ne\nUincentius him cw\u00e6\u00fe to mid cenum geleafum \u00feus, ne ondr\u00e6de ic me \u00feine witu ne \u00feine w\u00e6lhreowan\nDacianus \u00fea het hine gedon of \u00fe\u00e6re hengene, & hine eft ahon on heardum gealgan sona; & hine man\nMan ledde to his breostum feower brade isene clutas swi\u00f0e glowende \u00fe\u00e6t hit sang ongean, & hi \u00fea\nHim fleow \u00fea \u00fe\u00e6t blod ut ofer ealne \u00feone lichaman, & him se inno\u00fe eac geopenode ongean & his li\u00fea\nAc he eall \u00feis forb\u00e6r mid bli\u00feum andwlitan & mid strangum gaste on Godes andetnysse, to \u00feam\nWala wa, cw\u00e6\u00fe Datianus, we synd oferswi\u00f0ede.\nAc seca\u00fe nu, ic bidde, an blind cweart\u00e6rn \u00fe\u00e6r nan leoht ne mage inn, & on \u00feam myclum \u00feeostrum\nBeluca\u00f0 hine \u00feonne f\u00e6ste \u00fe\u00e6t he licge \u00fe\u00e6r ana leohtes bed\u00e6led on \u00feam la\u00f0um bedde.\nSecga\u00f0 me swa sona swa ge oncnawa\u00fe \u00fe\u00e6t he cucu ne by\u00f0.\n& \u00fea cwelleras swa dydon, gebrohton \u00feone halgan wer on \u00feam blindan cwearterne, & bes\u00e6ton hine\nMid \u00feam \u00f0e \u00fea weardmen wurdon on sl\u00e6pe, \u00fea com \u00fe\u00e6r heofonlic leoht into \u00feam halgan were on \u00feam\n\u00dea \u00f0a weardmen awocan, \u00fea wundrode \u00fea weardmen \u00fe\u00e6s wynsuman leohtes, swi\u00f0e afyrhte for \u00feam\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00fe se halga wer, of \u00feam heofonlican leohte ne beo ge afyrhte.\nIc heom nu gefrefrod mid engellicre \u00feenunge.\nGa\u00f0 in & sceawia\u00f0 hu me is.\nGe gebrohten me on \u00ferystum, & ic blissige nu on leohte; mine bendas sund tolysede, & ic blissige mid\nIc eom nu gestrangod & hnesce understreowod.\nWundria\u00f0 \u00feises, \u00fe\u00e6t se \u00fee wur\u00f0a\u00fe God mid so\u00fere andetnesse, \u00fe\u00e6t he sigef\u00e6st by\u00fe \u00e6fre.\nCy\u00fea\u00fe nu ardlice eowerum arleasan hlaforde hwilces leohtes ic bruce, & hwilcere beddinge, \u00fe\u00e6t he\nHis mildheortednesse ane ic me ondr\u00e6de swi\u00f0ost, \u00fe\u00e6t he beo awend swilce he wille me gemilscian.\nHi cyddon \u00fea \u00feis \u00feam hetolan cwellere, & he wear\u00f0 geangsumod on his mode & \u00e6bl\u00e6ce on nebbe\nBera\u00f0 hine nu, ic bidde, ut of \u00feam blindan cw\u00e6rterne to suman softan bedde \u00fe\u00e6t he mage swa hine\nNelle ic hine wyrcan wuldorfulran gyt, gif he on \u00feam witum gewitnod ateora\u00f0.\nHi hine namon and \u00fea b\u00e6ran bli\u00feelice on \u00e6armun \u00fee hine \u00e6r witnodon on \u00feam w\u00e6lhreowum\n& hi his fet cystun, & his flowende blod geornlice gaderoden him sylfum to h\u00e6le, & geleddon hine\nHit gelamp \u00fea sona \u00e6fter litlum fyrstum, \u00fe\u00e6t se halga diacon gewat of worlde to Gode mid\nDatianus \u00fea cw\u00e6\u00fe, se deofollica cweller\u00e6, ofsceamod swa\u00feeah, gif ic oferswi\u00f0an ne mihte hine \u00e6r\nAwyrpa\u00f0 nu his lic on anum widgillum felda, fugelum to \u00e6se, & fulum hundum to mete, & \u00feam\nSona geferedan \u00fe\u00e6t lic to \u00feam feldan middan, & hit \u00fear awurpon wildeorum and fugelum to mete, Hit\nSe \u00e6lmihtiga God \u00fee \u00fee Eliam his witegan \u00feurh \u00feone sweartan hr\u00e6m asende hwilon mete, on \u00feam\n\u00deis wear\u00f0 eft gecydd \u00feam arleasan Datiane, & he \u00fea geangsumod \u00feus cw\u00e6\u00fe, Ne m\u00e6g ic hine\nSwa ic his swi\u00f0or ehte mid swi\u00f0licre ehtnysse, swa ic hine swi\u00f0or wyrce wuldorfulran symle.\nAc gif \u00feeor\u00f0e ne m\u00e6g \u00feone mann forniman, be he besenced on s\u00e6licum y\u00f0um, \u00fe\u00e6t us swa oft ne\nBe he besiwod on anum s\u00e6cce mid hefegum stanum, & awurpa\u00f0 hine on \u00fe\u00e6re widgillan s\u00e6, \u00feam\n\u00d0a re\u00fean cwelleras \u00fea ra\u00fee swa dydon, awurpan \u00fe\u00e6s halgan lic on \u00fe\u00e6re widgillan s\u00e6, mid \u00feam\n\u00d0a hig swa gedon h\u00e6fdon, swa \u00f0e dema hi het.\n& reowan him hamweard mid healicre blisse.\nAc so\u00f0lice \u00fe\u00e6s halgan weres lic, \u00feurh \u00fees H\u00e6lendes mihte, to \u00feam strande becom \u00e6r\u00feam \u00fee hi stopon\nHis lic wear\u00f0 \u00fea geferod to geleaffulre cyrcan mid mycelre arwyr\u00f0nesse, & \u00fear on innan bebyriged; &",
